WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.920
Hey, welcome to Fascinating Frontiers, Episode 96.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:05.080
It's June 9th, 2026.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:06.840
The universe has been busy.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:07.960
Let's get into it.

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:13.000
Europeans start up Esar Aerospace just raised 270 million euros

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.240
to scale its rocket program worldwide.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.320
The German launch company secured the funding round

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:20.300
to prepare its next orbital attempt

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.180
and grow operations beyond Europe.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.220
Proceeds will support manufacturing,

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:26.700
scale up, and international market entry.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:29.140
The round values the firm at a level

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:32.680
that positions it among Europe's better capitalized new entrants.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.600
Esar's spectrum rocket remains on track

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.440
for a debut flight later this year.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.840
Next milestone watchers will track

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.060
as the outcome of that first launch attempt

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.260
and any new customer contracts announced afterward.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:48.840
Esar Aerospace's fresh capital arrives

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:52.100
as Europe tries to build a more competitive launch sector.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:56.040
The 270 million euros will fund both the next

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:58.760
spectrum test flight and factory expansion

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:00.160
needed for higher cadence.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.680
Success here would give the continent

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:05.120
a second medium lift option alongside

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:06.480
Arianne Group vehicles.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:09.740
Failure would reinforce how difficult it remains

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:12.560
for new entrants to reach reliable operations.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:16.040
The company's first orbital attempt later this year

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:17.540
will determine whether it can attract

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:19.220
follow-on government contracts.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.780
Now shifting to regulatory developments

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.040
in satellite networks.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.280
Regulators removed a looming construction milestone

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:29.940
that Amazon faced for its low-earth orbit broadband network.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:33.480
The waiver allows the company to continue deploying satellites

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:34.720
without immediate penalty.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:38.080
Official cited public interest in fostering

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:40.160
a second major broadband constellation

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.220
alongside existing operators.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:45.740
Amazon has already launched initial test satellites

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:47.100
and is ramping production.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.240
Observers will watch the pace of additional launches

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.920
and service rollout timelines in coming months.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:55.660
You know what is fascinating about this?

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:59.040
If every starlink satellite were the size of a city bus,

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:01.700
the entire constellation would still fit

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:04.440
inside a volume smaller than Earth atmosphere.

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:08.400
Each spacecraft flies in a carefully chosen orbital shell

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.560
where slight differences in altitude

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.960
and inclination create natural separation.

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:16.820
Operators fire tiny thrusters only when ground tracking

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:19.300
predicts a close approach measured in kilometers,

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:20.120
not meters.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:24.040
A single shell at 550 kilometers altitude

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:25.680
can hold thousands of satellites

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:28.840
because they move at 7.6 kilometers per second

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:31.600
and pass one another in fractions of a second.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.600
Yet the real puzzle is how the system scales

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:36.800
when adding another 10,000 satellites

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.800
requires predicting conjunctions years in advance

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:41.840
while accounting for solar activity

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.500
that changes atmospheric drag.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.360
No one yet knows the practical limit

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:49.360
before collision risk or radio interference forces

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:52.800
operators to thin the shells or move to higher orbits.

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:56.220
On a different note, Beijing has narrowed

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:58.820
commercial rocket providers eligible to fly

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:02.760
a new low-cost cargo spacecraft to the Tian Gong station.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.840
The move expands the role of private companies

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:07.720
in routine station resupply.

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:10.660
Selected entities will compete for missions

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:13.640
that previously relied solely on state rockets.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:16.040
The program aims to lower costs

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:18.660
while maintaining reliable delivery of supplies

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:19.480
and experiments.

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:22.880
Next steps include final selection of operators

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:24.620
and initial demonstration flights.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.280
China is also exploring commercial data purchases

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:30.620
rather than building every capability itself.

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:34.280
A new proposal suggests procuring satellite imagery

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.740
and analysis the same way governments already

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:38.880
buy weather or communications data.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:42.840
The approach would let agencies access commercial data sets

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:45.180
without building every capability in-house.

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:49.120
Recent open source analysis of Middle East imagery

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:52.140
by a Chinese firm highlighted the growing quality

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:53.240
of private products.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.400
Officials are weighing how such purchases could support

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.280
both civil and security needs,

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:00.660
watch for pilot procurement programs

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:02.800
and any policy changes that follow.

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:05.700
Institutional money continues to flow

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.720
into the broader space sector as well.

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:11.220
A subsidiary of the Taiwanese financial group plans

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:13.560
to participate in the upcoming public offering

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.600
of space exploration technologies.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:19.080
The move signals continued institutional interest

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:21.040
in the launch and satellite sector.

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:24.180
Details on share allocation remain limited

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.180
pending final IPO terms.

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:29.940
The listing would give public market investors direct exposure

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:32.060
to Starship and Starlink progress.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.320
Investors will monitor regulatory filings

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:37.680
for exact timing and valuation ranges.

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:41.440
Even as investors prepare for SpaceX's listing,

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:44.700
Rocket Labs CEO offered a blunt assessment

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:46.120
of who has truly scaled.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:48.900
The executive stated that just two companies

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:51.680
have reached high cadence orbital launch capability

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:53.080
at meaningful volume.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:56.860
One is SpaceX, the other remains unnamed in the remark.

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:59.700
The comment underscores how few players

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:01.620
have moved beyond sporadic missions.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:04.860
It comes as Rocket Lab itself pushes toward

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:07.540
more frequent electron and neutron flights.

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:10.680
Industry followers will track whether additional firms

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:12.480
close the gap in the next two years.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:15.320
Investors looking for broader exposure

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:16.960
now have a new fund option.

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:19.940
The asset manager introduced a new fund

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:23.020
focused on companies involved in launch, satellites,

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:24.540
and space infrastructure.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:28.060
The ETF gives investors broad exposure

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:29.820
without picking individual stocks.

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:33.340
It joins a growing list of sector-specific vehicles

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:35.080
tied to commercial space growth.

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:38.200
Assets under management and initial holdings

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:40.220
will be reported incoming disclosures.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.720
Performance relative to broader aerospace indices

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:45.160
will be watched closely.

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:48.220
While commercial activity dominates headlines,

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:51.760
the night sky still offers quiet observational treats.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:54.980
The two bright planets continue their close approach

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:56.300
visible after sunset.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:59.860
Venus officially passed north of Jupiter earlier today.

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:02.740
Observers can compare their relative brightness

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:05.040
and slight color difference with the naked eye

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:05.860
or binoculars.

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:09.500
The pairing will remain noticeable for several more evenings.

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:11.900
No special equipment is required

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:13.620
beyond a clear western horizon.

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:16.340
For those wanting deeper views,

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:19.240
a remarkable new image of the Rosette Nebula

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:20.260
has just been released.

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:23.540
A 200-hour image captured from Tennessee

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:25.900
shows fine tendrils of gas and dust

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:27.780
within the star-forming complex.

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:30.680
The portrait combines sulfur, hydrogen,

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:33.540
and oxygen filters through a five-inch telescope.

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:37.040
The Nebula lies roughly 5,000 light years away

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.180
in Montessaurus.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:42.280
Such long integrations highlight previously unseen filaments

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:44.000
where new stars are condensing.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:47.460
Similar deep surveys of other regions are planned

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:48.660
by the same imager.

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:52.080
Meanwhile, planning continues on flagship missions.

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:55.300
An astronaut photograph highlights urban development,

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:57.760
green corridors, and maritime traffic

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:00.000
around the Northern California metropolis.

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:03.260
The image shows how the city's layout interacts

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:05.080
with surrounding hills and the bay.

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:08.360
Such regular station imagery supports studies

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:10.980
of coastal urbanization and habitat change.

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:14.020
The crew continues adding to the long-running

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:15.480
Earth observation archive.

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:18.840
New passes over the region are expected in coming weeks.

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:22.080
New analysis of Sentinel 5P measurements

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:25.080
shows several regions decoupling rising prosperity

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:26.440
from worsening pollution.

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:29.080
The trend appears in cities that adopted

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:31.920
stricter emissions roles while expanding economically.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:35.860
Space-based monitoring provides consistent global coverage

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:38.280
that ground networks alone cannot match.

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:41.640
Researchers compared nitrogen dioxide levels

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:44.480
against GDP data over multiple years.

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:47.500
Follow-up studies will examine which policy

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.680
mixes produce the strongest improvements.

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:53.000
On the science planning front, agency officials

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:54.740
have begun outreach to lawmakers

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.700
about additional resources needed

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:58.600
to meet the current lunar timeline.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:01.700
The conversations focus on lander development

00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:03.260
and supporting infrastructure.

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:06.420
No formal budget request has been released yet.

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:09.640
Lawmakers will weigh the ask against other priorities

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:11.740
in upcoming appropriations debates.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:14.320
Progress on those talks will shape

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:17.720
whether the 2028 landing target stays realistic.

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:20.840
The virtual session will review science goals

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:24.180
and technology needs for the planned flagship mission.

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:26.460
Participants include astronomers

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:29.820
and instrument developers working on exoplanet characterization.

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:34.200
The 10AM PT start allows broad North American attendance.

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:37.260
Slides and recordings will be posted afterward

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:38.960
on the NASA science site.

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:42.840
Future seminars will drill into specific instrument concepts.

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:45.980
Keep an eye on those demonstration flights from China

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:48.400
as commercial cargo operations take shape.

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:51.540
That covers today's space and science news.

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:54.140
Share this with the fellow space enthusiast

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:55.280
if you found it interesting.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:56.980
I'm Patrick and Vancouver.

00:08:57.500 --> 00:08:57.980
See you tomorrow.

